el made by the folks at samsung  outputting at an aspect ratio of 21x9  with a native resolution of 3440 by 1440  means that if you're looking to stream  on this display the ultra wide format is  not in your favor qd here stands for  quantum dot display technology which  samsung has been focusing on to  challenge lg's dominance in the space  with this alienware monitor  samsung has found a champion for its  course  combine that with cinema grid color  coverage with 1000 nits peak brightness  and visa display hdr trueblack 400  certification this means gaming will  never look the same once you have laid  eyes on this monitor with g-sync  freesync 175 refresh rates and a 0.1 ms  response time alienware has ensured that  they won't be accused for cutting  corners at this price point  box wise we have display port 1.4 b  5 usb 3.2 ports and 2 hdmi 2.0 ports  facing downwards on the left yes in 2022  were still being provided hdmi 2.0 ports  in a premium monitor so if you're  looking to get the most out of this with  a ps5 or xbox series x it's best to  dampen those expectations because the pc  environment is where this alienware  monitor absolutely excels at talking  about pcs here's the word from today's  sponsor here at geek culture we love our  keyboards especially with the all new  logitech mx keys mini an elegant and  functional keyboard its ultra responsive  rounded keycaps are super stable and  quiet for more productivity there are  buttons to enable dictation microphone  audio control and emojis the backlit  keys illuminate when you get close and  matches the lighting of the environment  you're in it lasts up to 10 days on a  full charge or 5 months with the  backlights turned off to find out more  about the logitech mx keys mini and  their latest range of products head over  to logitech.com  and now let's head back to more chill  vibes  playing games at hdr turned up is an  experience that everyone should look  forward to at some point in the future  sadly not 